# Brahma — /run
# Requires: humao.rest-client

@brahma_host = localhost
@brahma_port = 8420
@base_url = http://{{brahma_host}}:{{brahma_port}}

# ── Zero-tool (text only, single turn) ──────────────────────────────────

### Hello World — zero tools, single-turn text response
POST {{base_url}}/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "task": "Say hello and introduce yourself in one sentence.",
  "max_turns": 3
}

### Simple question — one-word answer
POST {{base_url}}/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "task": "What is the capital of France? Answer in one word.",
  "max_turns": 3
}

# ── With tools ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Fibonacci — write + test via tools
POST {{base_url}}/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "task": "Write a Python function called 'fibonacci' that returns the nth Fibonacci number. Use write_file to save it to /tmp/fib.py, then verify it works by importing it with terminal.",
  "max_turns": 10
}

### One-liner with model override
POST {{base_url}}/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "task": "Write a 'hello world' Python script to /tmp/hello_brahma.py using write_file.",
  "model": "deepseek-chat",
  "max_turns": 5
}

# ── Bootstrap loop (forces capability generation) ───────────────────────

### Bootstrap — download image (no image tool → must generate one)
POST {{base_url}}/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "task": "I need to download the Python logo from python.org and save it locally. You do not have an image-download tool — bootstrap what you need. Write the tool code, test it, then use it to download https://www.python.org/static/img/python-logo.png to /tmp/python-logo.png.",
  "max_turns": 30
}

### Long-running — multi-file CLI project
POST {{base_url}}/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "task": "Create a complete Python CLI tool called 'notex' that takes markdown notes and saves them with timestamps. Write it to /tmp/notex/. Include tests in /tmp/notex/test_notex.py. Run the tests.",
  "max_turns": 40
}
